menuconfig LIBUKFI
	bool "ukfi: fault injection framework for Unikraft"
	default n
	select LIBUKDEBUG
	select LIBUKLIBPARAM
    select LIBUKSCHED
	# UK_CRASH() reaches uk_crash_trigger() through <uk/assert.h>, whose
	# arch-specific header is only on the include path when the crash
	# screen is on (see lib/ukdebug/Makefile.uk).
	select LIBUKPRINT
	select LIBUKDEBUG_CRASH_SCREEN
    help
        Fault injection for Unikraft components: marks points in the code
        where a fault can be introduced, and selects one of them at boot.

        Mark the points to test in the component's source:

            #include <uk/fi.h>
            UK_FI_SITE("name");            /* crash, hang, delay */
            UK_FI_SITE_ERR("name", -EIO);  /* also: return the error */

        Use UK_FI_SITE_ERR only where the function has a real failure
        path. Site names must be unique across the whole image: arming
        matches on the name alone, so duplicates are armed together.

        One image serves many experiments. The site, the fault type and
        the trigger are chosen at boot through libukfi.* parameters:

            -append "libukfi.fi_site=name libukfi.fi_fault=3 \
                     libukfi.fi_nop=5 -- <application arguments>"

        injects an error on the 5th call to that site. The injector
        lists every site it finds at boot with armed=0 or armed=1: that
        listing, not the command line, is the proof a parameter was
        understood, as unknown parameters are ignored without warning.

        The options below are build-time defaults only; the kernel
        parameters above override them at every boot.

        See lib/ukfi/README.md for the host-side campaign harness.

if LIBUKFI

config LIBUKFI_FI_SITE
	string "Default target operation (NULL disables)"
	default ""

config LIBUKFI_FI_NOP
	int "Default invocation at which the fault fires"
	default 1
	help
	  The fault fires from the n-th invocation of the site onwards.
	  A value above the number of times the site is actually invoked
	  arms the site and never fires: calibrate it on measured counts.

config LIBUKFI_FI_PERIOD
    int "Periodicity of the fault injection (0=disabled)"
    default 0
    help
      0 fires on every invocation from fi_nop onwards. A value k fires
      when (inv - fi_nop) is a multiple of k. Note that 0 does not mean
      "once": for crash and hang the difference is invisible, for error
      and delay it is not.

config LIBUKFI_FI_PROB
    int "Probability over 100000 of the fault injection (100000 is always)"
    default 100000
    help
      100000 skips the random draw entirely. Below that, one random
      state is shared by all sites, so a probabilistic run is only
      reproducible for a given seed with a single site armed.

config LIBUKFI_FI_SEED
    int "Seed for probabilistic triggers"
    default 1

config LIBUKFI_FI_FAULT
    int "Fault that is being injected (0=none, 1=crash, 2=hang, 3=error, 4=delay *delay is possible only if LIBUKSCHED is selected as well)"
    default 1

endif

if LIBUKGCOV

config LIBUKFI_GCOV_AFTER_MS
	int "Time in ms waited to exit the application for profiling purposes (0=disabled)"
	default 0
	help
	  Requests shutdown after the given time, so a server that never
	  exits on its own can still terminate cleanly - for a coverage
	  dump, or simply to bound an unattended run.

	  This belongs to the coverage helper, not to the injector: it is
	  available whenever LIBUKGCOV is on, including with LIBUKFI off.

endif
